{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Pohjois-Pohjanmaa lags the national share in crude curative treatment at 23.6% versus 27.0% nationally and in crude recorded multidisciplinary team meetings at 1.1% versus 6.0%.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:curative",
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Among 1050 new lung cancer patients in 2019–2023, the county's crude curative treatment share was 23.6% (95% CI 21.1–26.3; n=248/1050), where the 95% confidence interval excludes the national value of 27.0% (4009/14873), and these crude shares are not adjusted for age or stage.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In overlapping treatment categories where patients can receive multiple types, the crude life-prolonging share was 37.4% (95% CI 34.5–40.4; n=393/1050), with its 95% confidence interval excluding the national 30.4% (4522/14873), while the crude symptomatic share of 38.8% (95% CI 35.9–41.7; n=407/1050) has a 95% confidence interval that includes the national 39.5% (5871/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude share of patients with a multidisciplinary team meeting recorded in HILMO was 1.1% (95% CI 0.7–2.0; n=12/1050), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873), and this measures recording practice from direct patient contacts rather than actual multidisciplinary review.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The low crude curative share is unlikely to be only a recording artefact, but crude figures lack stage adjustment and public data omit key pathway timestamps.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The crude share with no treatment record within 12 months—mixing untreated patients and unrecorded treatment—is 25.0% (95% CI 22.5–27.8; n=263/1050), with its 95% confidence interval including the national 27.5% (4089/14873); as an inference, not a finding, this is consistent with relatively complete recording (not direct evidence), making the 23.6% crude curative share less likely to be only a recording artefact.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "cty:curative:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Although a figure digitised at ±0.5 percentage points shows national age-adjusted curative shares of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women, county shares here are crude, stage is missing for nearly half of new patients nationally, and a journal article's roughly 90% HILMO–Cancer Registry match covers diagnosis concordance only, not treatment or multidisciplinary recording.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While preliminary, unpublished national averages show 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland (56 days patient delay, 41 days primary care, 58 days specialist care), outpatient primary care visits and occupational health are not included in the report's data, which also lack timestamps for symptoms, referrals, imaging, first specialist visits, and treatment start.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist",
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "To address the lower crude curative share of 23.6%, the team recommends tracking THL 21/2016 access times, standardising referrals and diagnostic contacts, and auditing stage and multidisciplinary coding completeness.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act §52 sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national target access times are only planned for 2026–2028 (with Filha's diagnostics guideline due before the 2030 interim evaluation), the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers and flagging stalled handovers.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:24169121a4",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410",
          "q:432c0e51d6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Since patients are referred under local instructions, a mentor insight notes weak referrals receive lower specialist urgency ratings, and national referral criteria and care-coordinator guidance are only planned for 2026–2028 (for county adoption in 2029–2031), the team recommends a standard referral template, referring persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and naming a diagnostic-phase contact.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:0780bf74b0",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:29b792498e",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Given the county's 1.1% crude recorded multidisciplinary meeting share versus 6.0% nationally, missing stage data for nearly half of new patients nationally, and incomplete national reporting while a quality registry with 90% coverage is planned, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and multidisciplinary coding and reading gaps as data-quality signals first.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Pohjois_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:82d365cd2c",
          "q:990a0d39a0",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
